WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.925
Check the hardware before assembly.

00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:08.466
You will use a Phillips screwdriver and
the supplied Allen key, plus the screws,

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:12.900
bolts, hinge parts, bumper, and
four adjustable feet shown here.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.087
Steps 1 and 2.

00:00:15.087 --> 00:00:18.060
Lay the metal frame flat
on a protected surface.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.147
Slide the first side panel down
into the grooves, align the holes,

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:25.120
and fasten it with two of
the round-head screws.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.320
Steps 3 and 4.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.499
Fit the second side panel into
the opposite grooves the same way.

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:34.199
Make sure it sits fully down in the frame,

00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:37.220
then secure it with two
more round-head screws.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.476
Steps 5 and 6.

00:00:39.476 --> 00:00:44.691
Carefully roll the assembly over as shown
so the panels stay in their grooves.

00:00:44.691 --> 00:00:50.240
Fasten the lower panel edges with four
round-head screws, keeping the frame square.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.402
Steps 7 and 8.

00:00:52.402 --> 00:00:54.863
Slide the back panel into the open side,

00:00:54.863 --> 00:00:57.755
matching the shaped edges
shown in the drawing.

00:00:57.755 --> 00:01:01.940
Press the four side locks until they
click into the locked position.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.263
Steps 9 and 10.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:07.473
Drop the front panel into
the remaining opening,

00:01:07.473 --> 00:01:10.615
again matching the shaped
top and bottom edges.

00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:14.360
Press the four locking tabs
so the panel is held firmly.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.245
Step 11.

00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:22.164
Set the body upright onto the top frame
as shown, aligning the four corner holes.

00:01:22.164 --> 00:01:27.060
Use the Allen key to tighten four
threaded bolts through the frame.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:28.887
Step 12.

00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:32.502
Screw one adjustable foot into
each of the four leg ends.

00:01:32.502 --> 00:01:37.513
After all four are installed, carefully
turn the bedside table upright onto its

00:01:37.513 --> 00:01:37.830
feet.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.151
Steps 13 to 15.

00:01:40.151 --> 00:01:43.117
Lay the door flat with the inside facing up.

00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:48.374
Attach the handle with two screws, add
the small screw and washer near the top

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.340
corner, then press the bumper into its hole.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.206
Step 16.

00:01:53.206 --> 00:01:55.662
Choose which way the door will open.

00:01:55.662 --> 00:02:00.575
This build follows the first option
shown; the other option is mirrored.

00:02:00.575 --> 00:02:05.010
Press the lower hinge pin into
the front hole on the table frame.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.382
Steps 17 and 18.

00:02:07.382 --> 00:02:11.847
Lower the door onto the hinge pin
so the bottom corner sits on it.

00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:17.326
Slide the hinge fitting up into the top
corner and push it inward until it clicks

00:02:17.326 --> 00:02:17.800
locked.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:19.652
Step 19.

00:02:19.652 --> 00:02:24.279
Swing the door closed and check
that it sits evenly in the opening.

00:02:24.279 --> 00:02:29.873
Turn the four adjustable feet up or down
until the table stands level and steady,

00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:33.050
and remember the maximum
load is 25 kilograms.
